<p><code>pop-log</code> is a PSR-3 logger with six writers behind it. You compose a <code>Pop\Log\Logger</code> around one or
more writers, call <code>info()</code> or <code>error()</code> on it, and each writer decides where that entry lands — a file,
a syslog daemon, a database table, an inbox, an HTTP endpoint, or stdout. Swapping a laptop's log file
for a container's stdout is a change at construction and nowhere else.</p>
